#. type: TH
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "kernel_lockdown"
msgstr ""

#. type: TH
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "2026-02-10"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:10
msgid "kernel_lockdown - kernel image access prevention feature"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:16
msgid ""
"The Kernel Lockdown feature is designed to prevent both direct and indirect "
"access to a running kernel image, attempting to protect against unauthorized "
"modification of the kernel image and to prevent access to security and "
"cryptographic data located in kernel memory, whilst still permitting driver "
"modules to be loaded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:19
msgid ""
"If a prohibited or restricted feature is accessed or used, the kernel will "
"emit a message that looks like:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lockdown: X: Y is restricted, see man kernel_lockdown.7\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:28
msgid "where X indicates the process name and Y indicates what is restricted."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coverage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:33
msgid ""
"When lockdown is in effect, a number of features are disabled or have their "
"use restricted.  This includes special device files and kernel services that "
"allow direct access of the kernel image:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:36
msgid "/dev/mem"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:38
msgid "/dev/kmem"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:40
msgid "/dev/kcore"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:42
msgid "/dev/ioports"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:44
msgid "BPF"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:46
msgid "kprobes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:50
msgid ""
"and the ability to directly configure and control devices, so as to prevent "
"the use of a device to access or modify a kernel image:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:50 build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:53
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:55 build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:57
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:59 build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:61
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:63 build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:65
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:67 build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:69
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:71 build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:75
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:78 build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:81
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:84 build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[bu]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:53
msgid ""
"The use of module parameters that directly specify hardware parameters to "
"drivers through the kernel command line or when loading a module."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:55
msgid "The use of direct PCI BAR access."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:57
msgid "The use of the ioperm and iopl instructions on x86."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:59
msgid "The use of the KD*IO console ioctls."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:61
msgid "The use of the TIOCSSERIAL serial ioctl."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:63
msgid "The alteration of MSR registers on x86."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:65
msgid "The replacement of the PCMCIA CIS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:67
msgid "The overriding of ACPI tables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:69
msgid "The use of ACPI error injection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:71
msgid "The specification of the ACPI RDSP address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:73
msgid "The use of ACPI custom methods."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:75
msgid "Certain facilities are restricted:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:78
msgid ""
"Only validly signed modules may be loaded (waived if the module file being "
"loaded is vouched for by IMA appraisal)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:81
msgid ""
"Only validly signed binaries may be kexec'd (waived if the binary image file "
"to be executed is vouched for by IMA appraisal)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:84
msgid ""
"Unencrypted hibernation/suspend to swap are disallowed as the kernel image "
"is saved to a medium that can then be accessed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:87
msgid ""
"Use of debugfs is not permitted as this allows a whole range of actions "
"including direct configuration of, access to and driving of hardware."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:91
msgid ""
"IMA requires the addition of the \"secure_boot\" rules to the policy, "
"whether or not they are specified on the command line, for both the built-in "
"and custom policies in secure boot lockdown mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:93
msgid "The Kernel Lockdown feature was added in Linux 5.4."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/kernel_lockdown.7:105
msgid ""
"The Kernel Lockdown feature is enabled by CONFIG_SECURITY_LOCKDOWN_LSM.  The "
"I<lsm=lsm1,...,lsmN> command line parameter controls the sequence of the "
"initialization of Linux Security Modules.  It must contain the string "
"I<lockdown> to enable the Kernel Lockdown feature.  If the command line "
"parameter is not specified, the initialization falls back to the value of "
"the deprecated I<security=> command line parameter and further to the value "
"of CONFIG_LSM."
msgstr ""
